ASLONG FILE DONT CONTAIN "MARK:js-count-{{.block-name}}"

# ── Surface 3: Elixir (api compose) ──────────────────────────────────────────

# One compose_block/2 clause, inserted BEFORE the unknown-type catch-all
# (`def compose_block(%{"type" => type}, _style)`, compose.ex:1190) — clause
# order is load-bearing: anything after the catch-all is unreachable. The
# anchor is the END of the last typed clause (the chart email clause,
# compose.ex:1180-1181; `chart_email_html(b)` is unique, grep -cF = 1).
# Inserting AFTER it — rather than before the catch-all's comment — keeps the
# catch-all's own doc comment attached to its clause. render.ex is UNTOUCHED:
# render_block/2 (render.ex:182) is the entry point and dispatches every type
# through compose; it needs zero edits. Guard derives from the MARK line.
IN "api/lib/barkpark/portable_doc/render/compose.ex"
### Add the {{.block-name}} compose clause before the unknown-type catch-all
INSERT AFTER FIRST
::: last typed clause anchor :::
    %{"kind" => "_raw", "html" => Barkpark.PortableDoc.Render.DataViz.chart_email_html(b)}
  end
::: last typed clause anchor :::
WITH
::: {{.block-name}} compose clause :::

  # scaffy:add-block-type {{.BlockName}} MARK:ex-compose-{{.block-name}}
  # Starter compose for `{{.block-name}}`: the block's `text` attr escaped into
  # its bp-{{.block-name}} wrapper through the `_raw` pre-rendered-HTML hatch
  # (walk.ex passes `_raw` through verbatim — the same hatch ~68 sibling
  # clauses use). Every style gets the same div for now; replace with a real
  # Pd-node composition (see the `callout` clause for the PdCallout exemplar)
  # as the block grows semantics. `text` goes through the tolerant stringish/1
  # and Util.escape_html/1 so a raw API/SDK/CLI mutate can never break out of
  # the wrapper (papers are schemaless — same defense as the catch-all below).
  def compose_block(%{"type" => "{{.block-name}}"} = b, _style) do
    text = stringish(Map.get(b, "text", ""))

    %{
      "kind" => "_raw",
      "html" => ~s(<div class="bp-{{.block-name}}">) <> Util.escape_html(text) <> ~s(</div>)
    }
  end
::: {{.block-name}} compose clause :::
MARK "ex-compose-{{.block-name}}"

# ── Surface 4: golden-parity harness (closes the local-green/CI-red gap) ────

# The three surfaces above go green on every local ASSERT while CI still reds:
# doc-gates.yml runs scripts/pd-parity-completeness.sh on ANY **/*.ex diff
# (compose.ex is one), and that script counts compose.ex's dispatched types
# against a hard EXPECTED_COUNT pin — a new compose clause without a golden
# fixture + census bump = a CI red the local ASSERT list never exercised.
# This leg is REQUIRED (house doctrine — tests are never optional), and it is
# why the census crosses as a SECOND OPAQUE+SUCCESSOR pair: ParityCountBefore/
# After pin the compose-dispatch census (46 at authoring time), a different
# number line from the JS registry's CountBefore/After — the two pins move
# independently and only coincidentally both read 46 today.

# Parity fixture 1/3: one realistic authored input for the new type in the
# generator's hand-literal @inputs map. The anchor is the map's opening line
# (`@inputs %{`, gen_pd_parity.ex:81, grep -cF = 1). The sample MUST satisfy
# the compose clause Surface 3 writes: that clause reads exactly one attr —
# `text`, via stringish/1 — and a non-empty text is what keeps the frozen
# shape projection non-empty (pd_golden_parity_test.exs reds on an empty
# shape). Guard derives from the MARK line.
IN "api/lib/mix/tasks/barkpark.portable_doc.gen_pd_parity.ex"
### Add the {{.block-name}} parity input to the @inputs hand-literal map
INSERT AFTER FIRST
::: inputs map opening anchor :::
  @inputs %{
::: inputs map opening anchor :::
WITH
::: {{.block-name}} parity input :::
    # scaffy:add-block-type {{.BlockName}} MARK:parity-input-{{.block-name}}
    "{{.block-name}}" => %{"type" => "{{.block-name}}", "text" => "Parity starter text"},
::: {{.block-name}} parity input :::
MARK "parity-input-{{.block-name}}"

# Census pin 2/3: the completeness script's EXPECTED_COUNT. A REPLACE against
# the current count line (unique — every other mention reads $EXPECTED_COUNT).
# The target never survives in the replacement (ParityCountBefore ≠
# ParityCountAfter), but A4 hygiene still applies: the explicit ASLONG below
# matches the MARK line this op writes, and re-runs anchor at that mark. A
# second add-block-type run (a different block) is authored against the
# THEN-current census pair — its own mark stacks above the line.
IN "scripts/pd-parity-completeness.sh"
### Bump the completeness census pin from {{.ParityCountBefore}} to {{.ParityCountAfter}}
REPLACE
::: expected count anchor :::
EXPECTED_COUNT={{.ParityCountBefore}}
::: expected count anchor :::
WITH
::: {{.block-name}} completeness pin bump :::
# scaffy:add-block-type {{.BlockName}} MARK:parity-count-script-{{.block-name}}
EXPECTED_COUNT={{.ParityCountAfter}}
::: {{.block-name}} completeness pin bump :::
MARK "parity-count-script-{{.block-name}}"
ASLONG FILE DONT CONTAIN "MARK:parity-count-script-{{.block-name}}"

# Census pin 3/3: the parity suite's scope assertion (pd_golden_parity_test.exs
# :35 — `assert length(GenPdParity.types()) == N`, unique). Same REPLACE
# discipline as pin 2/3; the mark comment sits inside the test's do-block, a
# legal Elixir comment position.
IN "api/test/barkpark/portable_doc/render/pd_golden_parity_test.exs"
### Bump the parity suite census assert from {{.ParityCountBefore}} to {{.ParityCountAfter}}
REPLACE
::: census assert anchor :::
    assert length(GenPdParity.types()) == {{.ParityCountBefore}}
::: census assert anchor :::
WITH
::: {{.block-name}} census assert bump :::
    # scaffy:add-block-type {{.BlockName}} MARK:parity-count-test-{{.block-name}}
    assert length(GenPdParity.types()) == {{.ParityCountAfter}}
::: {{.block-name}} census assert bump :::
MARK "parity-count-test-{{.block-name}}"
ASLONG FILE DONT CONTAIN "MARK:parity-count-test-{{.block-name}}"

# ── Surface 5: downstream count-sync sites the generated golden set feeds ─────
# gen_pd_parity (Surface 4) writes ONE new golden into the js pd-golden dir; the
# golden-dir size IS the compose-dispatch census ({{.ParityCountBefore}} →
# {{.ParityCountAfter}}), so three DOWNSTREAM consumers that read that dir each
# pin the same +1. Two are hand-pinned test files this section bumps in place
# (sites 4 + 6, below); the third — the cloud vendored template copy (site 5) —
# is a byte-mirror re-synced by the `make cloud-templates-sync` ASSERT CMD, so it
# carries NO injected pin. The site-4 pins + site-6 corpus pin reuse the EXISTING
# ParityCount pair (they are the SAME golden-dir census, only LOOKING independent);
# only the site-6 textless pin needs its own TextlessSkip pair.

# ── Site 4: create-barkpark-app showcase seed (3 census pins) ────────────────
# The blog-starter's flagship post body is REGENERATED from the pd-golden set by
# scripts/gen-showcase-content.mjs (a Surface-5 ASSERT CMD); showcase-content.test.ts
# then guards seed≡goldens AND pins the census in THREE literal count assertions —
# each reds on the new golden until bumped. Same REPLACE+MARK+ASLONG discipline as
# the parity census pins (Surface 4). All three reuse the ParityCount pair.
IN "js/packages/create-barkpark-app/tests/showcase-content.test.ts"
### Bump the showcase goldens-length pin from {{.ParityCountBefore}} to {{.ParityCountAfter}}
REPLACE
::: showcase goldens-length anchor :::
    expect(goldens).toHaveLength({{.ParityCountBefore}})
::: showcase goldens-length anchor :::
WITH
::: {{.block-name}} showcase goldens pin :::
    // scaffy:add-block-type {{.BlockName}} MARK:showcase-goldens-{{.block-name}}
    expect(goldens).toHaveLength({{.ParityCountAfter}})
::: {{.block-name}} showcase goldens pin :::
MARK "showcase-goldens-{{.block-name}}"
ASLONG FILE DONT CONTAIN "MARK:showcase-goldens-{{.block-name}}"

IN "js/packages/create-barkpark-app/tests/showcase-content.test.ts"
### Bump the showcase seed-Set-size pin from {{.ParityCountBefore}} to {{.ParityCountAfter}}
REPLACE
::: showcase seed-set anchor :::
    expect(new Set(seedTypes).size).toBe({{.ParityCountBefore}})
::: showcase seed-set anchor :::
WITH
::: {{.block-name}} showcase seed-set pin :::
    // scaffy:add-block-type {{.BlockName}} MARK:showcase-seedset-{{.block-name}}
    expect(new Set(seedTypes).size).toBe({{.ParityCountAfter}})
::: {{.block-name}} showcase seed-set pin :::
MARK "showcase-seedset-{{.block-name}}"
ASLONG FILE DONT CONTAIN "MARK:showcase-seedset-{{.block-name}}"

IN "js/packages/create-barkpark-app/tests/showcase-content.test.ts"
### Bump the showcase distinct-renderings pin from {{.ParityCountBefore}} to {{.ParityCountAfter}}
REPLACE
::: showcase markers anchor :::
    expect(markersSeen.size).toBe({{.ParityCountBefore}})
::: showcase markers anchor :::
WITH
::: {{.block-name}} showcase markers pin :::
    // scaffy:add-block-type {{.BlockName}} MARK:showcase-markers-{{.block-name}}
    expect(markersSeen.size).toBe({{.ParityCountAfter}})
::: {{.block-name}} showcase markers pin :::
MARK "showcase-markers-{{.block-name}}"
ASLONG FILE DONT CONTAIN "MARK:showcase-markers-{{.block-name}}"

# ── Site 6: type-keyed toPlainText partition (2 pins + 1 classification) ──────
# toPlainText.typekeyed.test.ts reads the SAME pd-golden corpus and pins its size,
# and pins the PROSE/TEXTLESS partition. The starter has no `blockText` clause, so
# toPlainText returns '' for it — it is TEXTLESS, and the partition test reds
# unless the type is BOTH counted (textless pin +1) AND allow-listed (silent-drop
# ≠ intentional-skip). The prose half is UNTOUCHED (the starter extracts no prose);
# only the corpus pin (ParityCount) and the textless pin (TextlessSkip) move +1.

# Corpus-size pin — the SAME census as ParityCount (it counts the golden dir).
IN "js/packages/react/tests/toPlainText.typekeyed.test.ts"
### Bump the toPlainText corpus pin from {{.ParityCountBefore}} to {{.ParityCountAfter}}
REPLACE
::: typekeyed corpus anchor :::
    expect(cases.length).toBe({{.ParityCountBefore}})
::: typekeyed corpus anchor :::
WITH
::: {{.block-name}} typekeyed corpus pin :::
    // scaffy:add-block-type {{.BlockName}} MARK:typekeyed-corpus-{{.block-name}}
    expect(cases.length).toBe({{.ParityCountAfter}})
::: {{.block-name}} typekeyed corpus pin :::
MARK "typekeyed-corpus-{{.block-name}}"
ASLONG FILE DONT CONTAIN "MARK:typekeyed-corpus-{{.block-name}}"

# Textless-partition pin — an INDEPENDENT census (TextlessSkip): the prose half
# stays fixed while the textless half takes the +1. REPLACE against the current
# textless literal (unique — the prose line reads `PROSE_GOLDEN`, never TEXTLESS).
IN "js/packages/react/tests/toPlainText.typekeyed.test.ts"
### Bump the toPlainText textless-partition pin from {{.TextlessSkipBefore}} to {{.TextlessSkipAfter}}
REPLACE
::: typekeyed textless anchor :::
    expect(Object.keys(TEXTLESS_SKIP).length).toBe({{.TextlessSkipBefore}})
::: typekeyed textless anchor :::
WITH
::: {{.block-name}} typekeyed textless pin :::
    // scaffy:add-block-type {{.BlockName}} MARK:typekeyed-textless-{{.block-name}}
    expect(Object.keys(TEXTLESS_SKIP).length).toBe({{.TextlessSkipAfter}})
::: {{.block-name}} typekeyed textless pin :::
MARK "typekeyed-textless-{{.block-name}}"
ASLONG FILE DONT CONTAIN "MARK:typekeyed-textless-{{.block-name}}"

# The classification itself — the new type joins the TEXTLESS_SKIP allow-list.
# Anchor is the map's opening line (unique). The rationale states WHY it is
# textless AT BIRTH (no dispatch clause) and points to the grow move (manual
# step 7). Guard derives from the payload's MARK line (D3c — no ASLONG needed).
IN "js/packages/react/tests/fixtures/pd-plaintext-golden.ts"
### Classify {{.block-name}} into the TEXTLESS_SKIP allow-list
INSERT AFTER FIRST
::: textless-skip map anchor :::
export const TEXTLESS_SKIP: Record<string, string> = {
::: textless-skip map anchor :::
WITH
::: {{.block-name}} textless-skip entry :::
  // scaffy:add-block-type {{.BlockName}} MARK:plaintext-skip-{{.block-name}}
  '{{.block-name}}': 'starter block — no blockText dispatch clause yet, so toPlainText returns empty; move to PROSE_GOLDEN with a clause + golden when the block grows reading-flow prose (manual step 7)',
::: {{.block-name}} textless-skip entry :::
MARK "plaintext-skip-{{.block-name}}"

# ── Post-conditions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Per-surface file asserts — each string is a verbatim substring of what an op
# above writes (ASCII, brace-free).
ASSERT FILE "internal/pdrender/{{.block_name}}.go" CONTAINS "func ({{.blockName}}Renderer) Render(b Block, ctx RenderCtx) []string"
ASSERT FILE "internal/pdrender/{{.block_name}}_test.go" CONTAINS "func Test{{.BlockName}}Renderer(t *testing.T)"
ASSERT FILE "internal/pdrender/pdrender.go" CONTAINS "MARK:go-registry-{{.block-name}}"
ASSERT FILE "js/packages/react/src/blocks/core.ts" CONTAINS "MARK:js-emitter-{{.block-name}}"
ASSERT FILE "js/packages/react/src/blocks/core.ts" CONTAINS "MARK:js-map-{{.block-name}}"
ASSERT FILE "js/packages/react/tests/PortableDoc.test.tsx" CONTAINS "MARK:js-case-{{.block-name}}"
ASSERT FILE "js/packages/react/tests/PortableDoc.test.tsx" CONTAINS "toHaveLength({{.CountAfter}})"
ASSERT FILE "api/lib/barkpark/portable_doc/render/compose.ex" CONTAINS "MARK:ex-compose-{{.block-name}}"
ASSERT FILE "api/lib/mix/tasks/barkpark.portable_doc.gen_pd_parity.ex" CONTAINS "MARK:parity-input-{{.block-name}}"
ASSERT FILE "scripts/pd-parity-completeness.sh" CONTAINS "EXPECTED_COUNT={{.ParityCountAfter}}"
ASSERT FILE "api/test/barkpark/portable_doc/render/pd_golden_parity_test.exs" CONTAINS "== {{.ParityCountAfter}}"
# Surface 5 postconditions — the downstream census pins + the classification.
ASSERT FILE "js/packages/create-barkpark-app/tests/showcase-content.test.ts" CONTAINS "MARK:showcase-goldens-{{.block-name}}"
ASSERT FILE "js/packages/react/tests/toPlainText.typekeyed.test.ts" CONTAINS "cases.length).toBe({{.ParityCountAfter}})"
ASSERT FILE "js/packages/react/tests/toPlainText.typekeyed.test.ts" CONTAINS "TEXTLESS_SKIP).length).toBe({{.TextlessSkipAfter}})"
ASSERT FILE "js/packages/react/tests/fixtures/pd-plaintext-golden.ts" CONTAINS "MARK:plaintext-skip-{{.block-name}}"

# DRY-RUN HONESTY (benchmark note — read before you chase a phantom var bug).
# `bp scaffy run add-block-type … --dry-run` on THIS command ALWAYS reports
# ok:false, and that is COSMETIC, not a --var mistake. A dry-run executes
# nothing (D39: no writes, no ASSERT CMDs — the gen_pd_parity generator never
# runs), so the two golden-fixture `ASSERT FILE … EXISTS` lines above
# (the {{.block-name}}.golden.json pair) evaluate against a tree where those
# files were never generated: they are structurally ABSENT, the asserts fail,
# and ok goes false regardless of the vars. When you use the dry-run to METER
# the scaffold (engine-only wall-clock; tokens=0), read `duration_ms` from the
# structured envelope UNCONDITIONALLY — never gate the reading on ok or the exit
# code. A real (non-dry) run generates the pair via the gen_pd_parity ASSERT CMD
# BEFORE the EXISTS asserts evaluate, so there ok reflects the true post-apply
# state. (The starter golden then goes stale the moment you grow the block —
# manual step 6 above is its regen.)
#
# Gate commands. LOCAL tier = the proven-safe list only. The Go test run is the
# NAMED test (both Test{{.BlockName}}Renderer* functions match the -run prefix)
# — never the whole pdrender suite. The react vitest run (relocated to Surface 5,
# post-generation) is the fail-closed proof: it reds unless all four JS edits
# landed. Every Elixir gate is TIER ci until scoped local mix test is proven safe.
ASSERT CMD "go vet ./internal/pdrender/..."
ASSERT CMD "CC=/usr/bin/clang go build ./internal/pdrender/"
ASSERT CMD "go test ./internal/pdrender/ -run Test{{.BlockName}}Renderer -count=1"
# Precondition for every JS gate (D29): in a fresh worktree the js workspace has
# no node_modules and no built package dists — tsc reds with ~103
# cannot-find-module errors and vitest cannot resolve the workspace deps. One
# install + build greens them (proven: 103 errors -> 0, exit 0). The react vitest
# run is RELOCATED into Surface 5 (below): it must run AFTER gen_pd_parity mints
# the new golden, because toPlainText.typekeyed.test.ts pins `cases.length`
# against the LIVE pd-golden corpus and would red here on the old size.
# The build is scoped to react + its transitive deps (the `...` suffix), which
# resolves to exactly {@barkpark/core, @barkpark/react} (pnpm reports
# `Scope: 2 of 14`) — far cheaper than turbo-building the whole workspace. The
# `...` is MANDATORY: a bare
# `--filter @barkpark/react` omits @barkpark/core, whose dist react tsc needs,
# reintroducing the D29 TS2307 "Cannot find module @barkpark/core" false-red.
# `pnpm install` stays UNSCOPED (it must precede and hydrate the whole workspace).
ASSERT CMD "cd js && pnpm install && pnpm --filter @barkpark/react... build"
ASSERT CMD "cd js/packages/react && npx tsc --noEmit"
ASSERT CMD "cd api && mix test test/barkpark/portable_doc/render_test.exs" TIER ci
# Golden-parity leg (Surface 4). ONE gen run writes BOTH mirrors (proven —
# mirror_dirs() is the api fixtures dir + the js pd-golden dir); the EXISTS
# asserts sit between the CMDs on purpose: assertions execute in source order,
# so the pair is checked the moment the generator claims to have written it.
# The completeness script MUST run under bash (its shebang — zsh word-splits
# vacuously → false green), and the parity suite is the scoped single-file mix
# test A2 proved local-safe with a warm _build.
ASSERT CMD "cd api && MIX_ENV=test CC=/usr/bin/clang mix barkpark.portable_doc.gen_pd_parity"
ASSERT FILE "api/test/support/fixtures/pd-parity/{{.block-name}}.golden.json" EXISTS
ASSERT FILE "js/packages/react/tests/fixtures/pd-golden/{{.block-name}}.golden.json" EXISTS
ASSERT CMD "bash scripts/pd-parity-completeness.sh"
ASSERT CMD "cd api && CC=/usr/bin/clang mix test test/barkpark/portable_doc/render/pd_golden_parity_test.exs"

# ── Surface 5 gates: the downstream sync sites, all POST-generation ──────────
# Everything here reads the pd-golden corpus gen_pd_parity just minted (above),
# so it can only be validated once that golden exists. Running any of it before
# the generation step would red on a corpus of the OLD size — which is exactly
# the CI-only miss (compose-clause green locally, downstream red in CI) this
# amendment closes.

# The full react suite, RELOCATED from beside tsc. toPlainText.typekeyed.test.ts
# counts the LIVE pd-golden corpus (now {{.ParityCountAfter}}) and partitions it,
# so it greens only with the new golden present + the site-6 pins bumped.
# PortableDoc.test.tsx's registry count needs only the code injection and is happy
# here too. This is the fail-closed proof: it reds unless all four JS edits landed.
ASSERT CMD "cd js/packages/react && npx vitest run"

# Site 4 — regenerate the showcase seed from the now-{{.ParityCountAfter}} golden
# corpus, then run its pinned test. gen-showcase-content.mjs REWRITES
# templates/blog-starter/seeds/showcase-content.ts (a derived artifact,
# receipt-unowned — manual step 5 is its rollback); the test proves seed≡goldens
# and the three bumped census pins.
ASSERT CMD "cd js/packages/create-barkpark-app && node scripts/gen-showcase-content.mjs"
ASSERT CMD "cd js/packages/create-barkpark-app && npx vitest run"

# Site 5 — re-vendor the control-plane template copy from the regenerated seed,
# then prove no drift. `make cloud-templates-sync` byte-copies blog-starter +
# website-starter into cloud/priv/templates (derived, receipt-unowned — manual
# step 5 reverts it). The drift test is TIER ci (cloud mix env, heavyweight): CI
# runs BarkparkCloud.Templates.AppFilesDriftTest, the same both-directions gate.
ASSERT CMD "make cloud-templates-sync"
ASSERT CMD "cd cloud && mix test test/barkpark_cloud/templates/app_files_drift_test.exs" TIER ci
